cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  Beyond AUROC: quantifying calibration collapse in time-split
  validation of hepatotoxicity and cardiotoxicity models
message: Please cite this software using the metadata in this record.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Lee
    given-names: Noah
    alias: 이노아
version: v1.0
date-released: "2026-10-25"
# 개념 DOI 를 적는다. 버전 DOI 는 릴리스마다 Zenodo 가 새로 만들므로
# 여기에 박아 두면 바로 낡는다 (v0.1 의 버전 DOI 가 그랬다).
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.23583593
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/noahnoah0713/calibration-collapse-time-split"
abstract: >-
  Analysis code and results for two FDA toxicity datasets, DILIrank and
  DICTrank. Time-split validation degrades probability calibration far more
  than it degrades discrimination; the cause is decomposed into prevalence
  shift and a residual that survives matching both base rates; and yearly
  retraining followed by recalibration remains effective at label delays of
  up to five years.
keywords:
  - calibration
  - temporal validation
  - drug-induced liver injury
  - cardiotoxicity
  - distribution shift
  - reproducibility
